      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Labeled maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Single doses are usually capped at about 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** The order is about twice the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and include a clinical rationale for the order note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
